# Yu-Gi-Oh! Duel Monsters 4: Yuugi Deck (Japan) — dm4-hacking translation
# 4 MB GBC ROM. Primary small-ROM test fixture: 13 format patches,
# exercises CLI behavior, failure modes, and format coverage.
#
# NINJA1: wire format cross-validated against ninja-1.01php. PHP's
# encoder special-cases only {raw, snes, mega, gb} — it can't emit a
# patch flagged as GBC. Both encoders were run in raw mode for the
# four-quadrant cross-apply, then slap rebuilt the fixture with
# --rom-type gbc (single-byte diff at header byte 8: 0x00 → 0x05).

base:   test/data/dm4y/base.gbc
sha1:   b460119b0fbd80cecba3ded57fa11a16370dd43e
desc:   dm4y translation (4 MB GBC, 13 formats)

BPS      | test/data/dm4y/patch.bps       | converted | slap
IPS      | test/data/dm4y/patch.ips       | converted | slap
IPS32    | test/data/dm4y/patch.ips32     | converted | slap
UPS      | test/data/dm4y/patch.ups       | converted | slap
PPF3     | test/data/dm4y/patch.ppf       | converted | slap
EBP      | test/data/dm4y/patch.ebp       | converted | slap
APS-N64  | test/data/dm4y/patch.aps       | converted | slap
NINJA1   | test/data/dm4y/patch.ninja1    | converted | slap
NINJA2   | test/data/dm4y/patch.rup       | converted | slap
GDIFF    | test/data/dm4y/patch.gdiff     | converted | slap
VCDIFF   | test/data/dm4y/patch.vcdiff    | converted | xdelta3 -S none
bsdiff   | test/data/dm4y/patch.bsdiff    | converted | bsdiff
xdelta1  | test/data/dm4y/patch.xdelta1   | converted | xdelta 1.1.4
